</span></strong><span class=3D"">.</span></p><h2><span class=3D"">The Hones=
t Answer: You Don't </span><em><span class=3D"">Need</span></em><span class=
=3D""> Neural Networks</span></h2><p class=3D"ds-markdown-paragraph"><span =
class=3D"">For CIC-IDS2017/2019 datasets, Random Forest and LightGBM consis=
tently achieve </span><strong><span class=3D"">96-99% accuracy</span></stro=
ng><span class=3D""> when properly tuned. CNNs typically achieve </span><st=
rong><span class=3D"">97-99.3%</span></strong><span class=3D""> on the same=
 datasets. The 0.3-1% gain is rarely worth the added complexity.</span></p>=
<p class=3D"ds-markdown-paragraph"><strong><span class=3D"">However</span><=
/strong><span class=3D"">, you mentioned behavioral detection is your main =
concern. This changes the equation significantly.</span></p><hr><h2><span c=
lass=3D"">Pattern-Based vs Behavioral-Based Detection: Where Models Excel</=
span></h2><h3><span class=3D"">Pattern-Based (Signature/Feature-Based)</spa=
n></h3><ul><li><p class=3D"ds-markdown-paragraph"><strong><span class=3D"">=
Definition:</span></strong><span class=3D""> Detecting known attacks by mat=
ching specific feature values (e.g., "SYN flood =3D high SYN count, low ACK=
 count")</span></p></li><li><p class=3D"ds-markdown-paragraph"><strong><spa=
n class=3D"">What works:</span></strong><span class=3D""> Both classical ML=
 and deep learning perform equally well</span></p></li><li><p class=3D"ds-m=
arkdown-paragraph"><strong><span class=3D"">Winner:</span></strong><span cl=
ass=3D""> Tie =E2=80=94 both easily exceed 90%</span></p></li></ul><h3><spa=
n class=3D"">Behavioral-Based (Sequential/Contextual)</span></h3><ul><li><p=
 class=3D"ds-markdown-paragraph"><strong><span class=3D"">Definition:</span=
></strong><span class=3D""> Detecting anomalies in communication patterns o=
ver time (e.g., "Server normally sends 50KB/s outbound, suddenly sending 50=
0MB/s at 3 AM")</span></p></li><li><p class=3D"ds-markdown-paragraph"><stro=
ng><span class=3D"">What works:</span></strong><span class=3D""> This is wh=
ere time-series and sequence modeling matters</span></p></li><li><p class=
=3D"ds-markdown-paragraph"><strong><span class=3D"">Winner:</span></strong>=
<span class=3D""> Depends on your implementation approach</span></p></li></=
ul><hr><h2><span class=3D"">When Neural Networks Actually Help with Behavio=
ral Detection</span></h2><p class=3D"ds-markdown-paragraph"><span class=3D"=
">Random Forest treats each flow as </span><strong><span class=3D"">indepen=
dent</span></strong><span class=3D"">. Behavioral detection requires </span=
><strong><span class=3D"">context across multiple flows</span></strong><spa=
n class=3D"">. Here's where the difference matters:</span></p><div class=3D=
