t"><p class=3D"ds-markdown-paragraph"><span class=3D"">Yes, but with import=
ant caveats. The scaling challenge isn't about model capacity =E2=80=94 it'=
s about </span><strong><span class=3D"">operational complexity</span></stro=
ng><span class=3D"">, not algorithmic limitations.</span></p><hr><h2><span =
class=3D"">Where RF Remains Valid at Large Scale</span></h2><p class=3D"ds-=
markdown-paragraph"><strong><span class=3D"">Detection capability doesn't d=
egrade with scale.</span></strong><span class=3D""> A well-tuned Random For=
est can distinguish malicious from benign flows whether you're processing 1=
00 flows/minute or 1 million flows/minute. The math doesn't change.</span><=
/p><p class=3D"ds-markdown-paragraph"><span class=3D"">Large enterprises st=
ill use RF-based detection successfully in:</span></p><ul><li><p class=3D"d=
s-markdown-paragraph"><strong><span class=3D"">Splunk Enterprise Security:<=
/span></strong><span class=3D""> Their ML Toolkit defaults to Random Forest=
 and Isolation Forest. They handle petabytes daily across Fortune 500 SOCs.=
</span></p></li><li><p class=3D"ds-markdown-paragraph"><strong><span class=
=3D"">Elastic Security:</span></strong><span class=3D""> Uses ensemble tree=
 methods for their prebuilt detection jobs, deployed across massive cluster=
s.</span></p></li><li><p class=3D"ds-markdown-paragraph"><strong><span clas=
s=3D"">Multiple financial institutions:</span></strong><span class=3D""> Se=
veral large banks I'm aware of run RF-based anomaly detection on SWIFT and =
internal network traffic at 100K+ events/second.</span></p></li></ul><p cla=
ss=3D"ds-markdown-paragraph"><span class=3D"">The model itself isn't the bo=
ttleneck.</span></p><hr><h2><span class=3D"">What Actually Breaks at Large =
Enterprise Scale</span></h2><h3><span class=3D"">1. Training Data Fragmenta=
tion</span></h3><p class=3D"ds-markdown-paragraph"><span class=3D"">A mid-s=
ize company has one network pattern. A multinational has 47 offices, each w=
ith different normal behavior. The manufacturing plant in Germany looks not=
hing like the trading floor in Singapore.</span></p><p class=3D"ds-markdown=
-paragraph"><span class=3D"">You can't train one global RF model. You need =
per-site or per-segment models, or a hierarchical approach where local mode=
ls feed a global aggregator. This is an architecture problem, not a model s=
election problem.</span></p><h3><span class=3D"">2. Concept Drift Velocity<=
/span></h3><p class=3D"ds-markdown-paragraph"><span class=3D"">Network beha=
vior changes faster in large environments. New applications deploy weekly. =
Mergers integrate foreign networks. Cloud migration shifts traffic patterns=
.</span></p><p class=3D"ds-markdown-paragraph"><span class=3D"">RF handles =
drift better than neural networks, but the retraining cadence becomes the b=
ottleneck =E2=80=94 not model training time, but labeling new data fast eno=
ugh. Large enterprises solve this with dedicated threat hunting teams that =
continuously produce labeled data.</span></p><h3><span class=3D"">3. Featur=
e Engineering Maintenance</span></h3><p class=3D"ds-markdown-paragraph"><sp=
an class=3D"">The 80+ CicFlowMeter features might work for one environment =
but miss signals in another. A large enterprise might need different featur=
e sets for:</span></p><ul><li><p class=3D"ds-markdown-paragraph"><span clas=
s=3D"">Campus user traffic</span></p></li><li><p class=3D"ds-markdown-parag=
raph"><span class=3D"">Data center east-west traffic</span></p></li><li><p =
class=3D"ds-markdown-paragraph"><span class=3D"">Cloud egress</span></p></l=
i><li><p class=3D"ds-markdown-paragraph"><span class=3D"">OT/IoT networks</=
span></p></li><li><p class=3D"ds-markdown-paragraph"><span class=3D"">VPN t=
ermination points</span></p></li></ul><p class=3D"ds-markdown-paragraph"><s=
pan class=3D"">Maintaining consistent feature extraction across these is th=
e real operational cost. RF works fine =E2=80=94 if you can keep the featur=
e pipeline consistent and relevant everywhere.</span></p><h3><span class=3D=
"">4. Alert Volume, Not Detection Accuracy</span></h3><p class=3D"ds-markdo=
wn-paragraph"><span class=3D"">Here's the actual large-enterprise bottlenec=
k:</span></p><div class=3D"md-code-block md-code-block-dark"><div class=3D"=
